{
  "area": "ui-notifications",
  "description": "The notifications view-models (Features WV1, P2.core; CROSS-ENGINE-FEATURES §4, 2. HUD shell; catalog ui-notifications): the toast queue (core src/ui/notifications.ts Notifications, mirrored by Godot insimul_notifications.gd and Unreal FInsimulNotifications) and the history log behind the collapsed HUD feed and the Notifications tab (core src/game-engine/logic/NotificationStore.ts NotificationLog, the NotificationStore singleton's class). Runner: src/ui/hud-corpus.ts. Op toasts runs steps {push:{text,kind?,lifetime?}} -> {id}, {tick:seconds} -> {changed}, {dismiss:id} -> {removed}, {clear:true} -> {} on a new queue and pins every result, the visible list and the count. Op history runs steps on a new log whose clock reads the last step's at (ms, 0 before any): {push:{title,description?,icon?,color?,category?}} -> {id}, {pushMany:{count,title,category?}} pushes \"<title> <k>\" for k = 0..count-1 -> {firstId,lastId}, {recent:n} and {all:true} -> {items} (or {ids} with ids:true), {length:true}, {clear:true}. Every case is {name, op, input, expected}; numbers compare within tolerance, everything else exactly, object key sets included (a key TypeScript leaves undefined is absent). A non-finite number is written as null in an input. Regenerate with npm run hud-corpora; npm run hud-corpora:check fails on any difference.",
  "version": 1,
  "sources": [
    "Rules are core main's, unchanged: Notifications (US-GU1) and NotificationStore (moved from Babylon earlier); P2.core only exports the log's class with an injectable clock and cap.",
    "Inputs are synthetic."
  ],
  "tolerance": 1e-9,
  "contract": {
    "kinds": [
      "info",
      "success",
      "warning",
      "danger"
    ],
    "kindColor": {
      "info": "accent",
      "success": "success",
      "warning": "warning",
      "danger": "danger"
    },
    "defaultLifetimeSeconds": 4,
    "toastFirstId": 1,
    "toastExpiry": "a toast is dropped by the tick that takes its remaining time to 0 or below",
    "historyFirstId": 0,
    "historyMax": 200,
    "historyOrder": "newest first",
    "categories": [
      "quest",
      "system",
      "building",
      "npc",
      "item",
      "skill",
      "general"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
